 "X113": {"key": "t-star", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "a find pays once (N347): your unit standing by a fallen star for ten seconds gains its 300 iron and 100 gold once, and the star is marked taken", "cite": ["N347"]},
 "X114": {"key": "t-n42", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N46, from N42 (N349-N351): a bulk sale at the Market sells 1,000 wood in one tap for less than ten single lots; an untimed game shows no countdown under the clock and a standing wonder shows its own; after the page was hidden and the old sound player will not resume, the next tap makes a new one; a research cell shows what it gives; a bush picked out stays, bare, and is back past six tenths after the turn of spring", "cite": ["N349", "N350", "N351", "N353"]},
 "X115": {"key": "t-n43", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N46, from N43 (N355, N357, N359): the sea holds fish of the book's amount along every coast and at least nine in ten of the fish by the coast have a place to stand (N361; under six in ten before); a building goes up in three stages: a slab only at a twentieth built, the frame half raised and nothing filled at about a third, the frame whole and the building half filled at three quarters, and a plot too low for a frame goes from slab to filling; a villager whose way runs through the woods is not asked how to cross them, a soldier is", "cite": ["N355", "N357", "N359", "N361"]},
 "X117": {"key": "t-n47", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N47 (N362-N364): Z4 by the randomizer: six rich clearings, one for every pair of homes, each with both homes of its pair no more than a third farther than the nearest home, each holding the home pocket's gold, stone, iron and berries and room for a Mill, a Mine and a Tower three times over; plain clearings beside them; no tree stands in a clearing; every clearing, the middle and every home are joined by ground free of trees; a tree holds four villagers and is full to a fifth", "cite": ["N362", "N363", "N364"]},
 "X118": {"key": "t-n48", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N48 (N365): dock + fish, one element: a dock laid by wild fish holds two spots' worth of its own plus every wild spot in its reach, each counted once; a wild spot is no find to anyone by itself; a villager tapped onto one is sent to the dock, fishes there and lands the catch; fished out, the dock keeps a quarter, rests bare and lets its worker go; at the turn of spring it is back", "cite": ["N365"]},
 "X119": {"key": "t-n49", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N49 (N366): the mine shaft: before Blasting a Mining camp is only a drop-off; after it, the camp is a post that yields gold: a villager tapped onto it works there and gold comes into the stores with no carrying, its stock falling; emptied, it can be sunk again for its price's share and is full", "cite": ["N366"]},
 "X120": {"key": "t-n50", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N50 (N367): the Pioneer: locked until Pioneer corps is learned; it may enter the woods where a Ram may not; standing still it fells nothing; moving, it fells the trees in its lane: a felled tree is still there with all its wood, is no longer woods, and lets a Ram through; a villager tapped onto it gathers it; trees out of its lane stand", "cite": ["N367"]},
 "X121": {"key": "t-n51", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N51 (N368): an order to ground is obeyed in a fight: eight foot and eight archers fighting an equal force are sent to empty ground; three seconds on none is still on a foe and at least four in five of those who have not broken are nearer the spot; twelve seconds later none of those has turned back to the fight (a soldier who breaks and runs is no longer under the order: the nerve law, not this one)", "cite": ["N368"]},
 "X122": {"key": "t-n52", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N52 (N369): a chosen option's ring is whole (its box above its neighbours, the ring the size of the box it is laid on); the Town Center page does not rest the world; a building's card lists no research of a later age until Show tech is on; a research of this age waiting on another opens that one's building with its box ringed, or the Build page on the building when none stands; three sites placed in a row are one villager's, built in the order placed, + Villager sends a second, and a villager tapped onto a site takes that site; every research ring is blue, lit when it can start, green while it runs; a price is white at exactly enough and green at twice; a tap on open ground opens nothing; the home patch holds half again as many bushes; a trained unit comes out on the south side and stands in a yard to the south; a Mint may touch a Mint and a Dwelling a Dwelling, never a Barracks; N62 (N385) moved three checks to the Nov 15 rulings: Show tech is cut (a later age's research stays hidden); in the dock a research rings only at work (green while it runs); the price's colour ticks in steps", "cite": ["N369", "N385"]},
 "X123": {"key": "t-n53", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N53 (N370): a Wonder cannot be laid before the last open age and can in it; laying one tells every side, with its place; one villager's four minutes leave it under a fifth raised; a finished one wins only after 1,000 s; a computer waits for the last open age too; Exit (one villager or the called group) kills through the one death path: gone from the board and the head count (N371)", "cite": ["N370", "N371"]},
 "X124": {"key": "t-n54", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N54 (N372): the trade roads: every land tile along both routes, far stop to far stop, wears to dirt (none grass), no tree stands on them, and every stop sits on its road; inside 200 feet of a road only oaks stand (Statute of Winchester); a free stop draws its empty trade booth and a held one leaves the drawing to its Trade post (N375)", "cite": ["N372", "N373", "N374", "N375"]},
 "X125": {"key": "t-n55", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N55 (N376, N377): spy, medic and priest are the army (class Support): a picked priest tapped on an enemy goes to convert him, a spy on an enemy building goes to sabotage it, a medic goes where he is sent; no message bar: a message is a letter in Mail, and no menu carries a help line", "cite": ["N376", "N377"]},
 "X126": {"key": "t-n56", "value": {"stage": "retired", "why": "the two look buttons; the alert circle sits by W (Design 14; t-n67)", "by": "N71"}, "name": "N56 (N378): two look buttons on the top row: the banner cycles the camera through the army's fronts and round again, the alert jumps to what of mine is under attack", "cite": ["N378", "N395"]},
 "X127": {"key": "t-n57", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N57 (N379), N58 (N381), N59 (N382): no drawn road runs in water; stops keep apart and clear of every find; the trade roads reach the water at both sides of the map (one road or two per route); each trade road winds: somewhere it strays more than two tiles from the straight line between its stops; its ground is not grass; every stop lies on a road; the research tab (v80's parchment pill) marks a building with research ready, at its roof's upper left corner", "cite": ["N379", "N380", "N381", "N382"]},
