 "X141": {"key": "t-n71", "value": {"stage": "page"}, "name": "N71 (N395; Design 18, the Nov 18 audit fixes): an idle villager is one thing (the Idle box, the tip and the send-an-idle-villager verb read ECON.idlers; a garrisoned villager is none of them); the menu draws every icon from the Screen book; the refusals read from the Words book (a blocked site, a full line, no villagers); the new game's options keep their words and values; a find with a yield is told by its Yield tick; Carry and Repair are ticked nowhere", "cite": ["N395"]}
